1
00:00:02,257 --> 00:00:04,257
♪

2
00:00:04,257 --> 00:00:05,557
Asuna: TAKE ME TO KIRITO.

3
00:00:08,477 --> 00:00:10,437
Higa: WELL, THERE YOU GO.

4
00:00:10,437 --> 00:00:12,857
I TOLD YOU YOUR BOY
WAS THE BIGGEST THREAT

5
00:00:12,857 --> 00:00:14,477
TO THIS PROJECT’S SECURITY.

6
00:00:14,477 --> 00:00:16,897
Kikuoka: I KNOW.
YOU DON’T HAVE TO RUB IT IN.

7
00:00:16,897 --> 00:00:19,027
Asuna: IS KIRITO
EVEN SAFE HERE?!

8
00:00:19,027 --> 00:00:21,487
WERE YOU LYING WHEN YOU SAID
YOU COULD SAVE HIM?

9
00:00:21,487 --> 00:00:24,407
IS HE ALIVE?! ANSWER ME!

10
00:00:24,407 --> 00:00:26,907
( Kikuoka sighs )

11
00:00:26,907 --> 00:00:29,747
KANEMOTO INJECTED
A POTENT TOXIN INTO HIM.

12
00:00:29,747 --> 00:00:32,127
IT DAMAGED
KIRITO’S BRAIN SO MUCH,

13
00:00:32,127 --> 00:00:34,417
CONVENTIONAL TREATMENT
CAN’T HEAL HIM.

14
00:00:34,417 --> 00:00:35,707
( Asuna shudders )

15
00:00:35,707 --> 00:00:38,587
Kikuoka: BUT
UNCONVENTIONAL TREATMENT CAN,

16
00:00:38,587 --> 00:00:41,127
AND THE ONLY PLACE
WITH THAT TECHNOLOGY IS RATH.

17
00:00:41,127 --> 00:00:42,467
( Asuna gasps )

18
00:00:42,467 --> 00:00:44,137
Kikuoka: I’M SURE
HE TOLD YOU ABOUT IT,

19
00:00:44,137 --> 00:00:47,637
THE S.T.L.,
SHORT FOR "SOUL TRANSLATOR."

20
00:00:47,637 --> 00:00:51,597
IF WE USE THE S.T.L.
TO STIMULATE HIS FLUCTLIGHT,

21
00:00:51,597 --> 00:00:53,267
WE CAN REGENERATE
A BRAND-NEW,

22
00:00:53,267 --> 00:00:55,397
PERFECTLY HEALTHY
NEURAL NETWORK,

23
00:00:55,397 --> 00:00:56,817
BUT THAT TAKES TIME.

24
00:00:56,817 --> 00:00:59,897
RIGHT NOW,
HE’S IN A FULL-SPEC S.T.L.,

25
00:00:59,897 --> 00:01:02,027
WHICH CAN ONLY BE FOUND HERE.

26
00:01:02,027 --> 00:01:03,527
THE TREATMENT HE’S GETTING

27
00:01:03,527 --> 00:01:06,327
SURPASSES WHAT
ANY HOSPITAL CAN OFFER.

28
00:01:06,327 --> 00:01:09,497
HE EVEN HAS
HIS OWN FULL-TIME NURSE.

29
00:01:09,497 --> 00:01:12,117
Asuna: OKAY, THEN.
I’LL TAKE YOUR WORD FOR IT.

30
00:01:13,497 --> 00:01:15,127
Rinko: ALL RIGHT, KIKUOKA.

31
00:01:15,127 --> 00:01:16,837
SINCE YOU’RE
IN THE MOOD TO TALK,

32
00:01:16,837 --> 00:01:19,337
MIGHT AS WELL TELL US
EVERYTHING FROM THE TOP.

33
00:01:19,337 --> 00:01:22,337
FIRST, WHY IS
AN S.D.F. OFFICIAL LIKE YOU

34
00:01:22,337 --> 00:01:24,047
USING THE MINISTRY AS A FRONT?

35
00:01:24,047 --> 00:01:26,557
NEXT, WHAT’S THE POINT OF THIS?

36
00:01:26,557 --> 00:01:29,677
AND LAST,
WHY KIRIGAYA, SPECIFICALLY?

37
00:01:29,677 --> 00:01:32,767
Kikuoka: IF YOU WANT ANSWERS,
YOU’LL HAVE TO SIGN ON.

38
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:33,807
Rinko: HOW ’BOUT
YOU START TALKING?

39
00:01:35,607 --> 00:01:37,687
Kikuoka: ALL RIGHT, THEN.

40
00:01:37,687 --> 00:01:40,647
I ASSUME YOU’RE BOTH FAMILIAR
WITH THE CONCEPT OF THE S.T.L.?

41
00:01:40,647 --> 00:01:43,067
Asuna: IT READS SOULS,

42
00:01:43,067 --> 00:01:44,817
OR FLUCTLIGHTS,
AS YOU CALL THEM,

43
00:01:44,817 --> 00:01:46,657
AND ALLOWS THE USER TO DIVE

44
00:01:46,657 --> 00:01:48,867
INTO A VIRTUAL WORLD
THAT’S INCREDIBLY LIFELIKE.

45
00:01:48,867 --> 00:01:51,827
Kikuoka: THAT’S CORRECT.
AND DO YOU KNOW

46
00:01:51,827 --> 00:01:54,457
WHAT THE OBJECTIVE
OF THIS PROJECT IS?

47
00:01:54,457 --> 00:01:55,247
Asuna: NO, I DON’T.

48
00:01:57,417 --> 00:01:58,957
Kikuoka: TO CREATE A BOTTOM-UP,

49
00:01:58,957 --> 00:02:01,837
MULTIPURPOSE
ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE.

50
00:02:01,837 --> 00:02:03,337
♪

51
00:02:03,337 --> 00:02:05,887
♪ SHINY SWORD, MY DIAMOND ♪

52
00:02:05,887 --> 00:02:07,507
( singing in Japanese )

53
00:02:18,647 --> 00:02:19,647
♪ IT’S TIME ♪

54
00:02:19,647 --> 00:02:21,487
( singing in Japanese )

55
00:02:37,747 --> 00:02:42,007
♪

56
00:03:36,007 --> 00:03:39,717
Asuna: A BOTTOM-UP,
MULTIPURPOSE A.I.?

57
00:03:39,717 --> 00:03:41,087
Kikuoka: THAT’S RIGHT.

58
00:03:41,087 --> 00:03:43,507
THERE ARE TWO APPROACHES
TO DEVELOPING AN A.I.

59
00:03:43,507 --> 00:03:46,637
THE FIRST IS CALLED TOP-DOWN
ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE,

60
00:03:46,637 --> 00:03:48,887
WHERE THE A.I. IS PROGRAMMED
WITH EXPERIENCE AND KNOWLEDGE

61
00:03:48,887 --> 00:03:50,597
SO THAT IT LEARNS ENOUGH

62
00:03:50,597 --> 00:03:52,727
TO APPROACH SOMETHING
CLOSE TO TRUE INTELLIGENCE.

63
00:03:52,727 --> 00:03:54,607
Higa: THAT’S PRETTY MUCH
THE GIST OF IT.

64
00:03:54,607 --> 00:03:56,357
EVERYTHING
THAT’S AN A.I. RIGHT NOW

65
00:03:56,357 --> 00:03:58,027
IS USING THAT TOP-DOWN APPROACH.

66
00:03:58,027 --> 00:04:01,197
HECK, DR. SHIGEMURA WAS
WORKIN’ WITH US HERE FOR A BIT,

67
00:04:01,197 --> 00:04:03,527
AND EVEN HIS RESEARCH
FOCUSED ON THAT.

68
00:04:03,527 --> 00:04:05,447
Kikuoka:
A TOP-DOWN A.I., HOWEVER,

69
00:04:05,447 --> 00:04:06,827
CAN’T REACT APPROPRIATELY

70
00:04:06,827 --> 00:04:08,827
TO THINGS
IT HASN’T LEARNED ABOUT.

71
00:04:08,827 --> 00:04:10,537
AT THIS POINT IN TIME,

72
00:04:10,537 --> 00:04:12,667
NONE HAVE EVOLVED ENOUGH
TO HAVE TRUE INTELLIGENCE.

73
00:04:14,587 --> 00:04:16,547
THE SECOND APPROACH
TO A.I. DEVELOPMENT

74
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:18,007
IS CALLED BOTTOM-UP.

75
00:04:18,007 --> 00:04:20,127
THE HUMAN BRAIN IS AN ORGAN

76
00:04:20,127 --> 00:04:22,007
COMPRISED
OF ONE HUNDRED BILLION CELLS

77
00:04:22,007 --> 00:04:24,007
CONNECTED IN INTRICATE WAYS.

78
00:04:24,007 --> 00:04:25,757
THE IDEA OF BOTTOM-UP

79
00:04:25,757 --> 00:04:27,887
IS RECREATING THE BRAIN
ELECTRONICALLY

80
00:04:27,887 --> 00:04:29,977
AND GENERATING
TRUE INTELLIGENCE IN IT.

81
00:04:29,977 --> 00:04:31,937
Asuna: BUT THAT
WOULD BE IMPOSSIBLE TO DO.

82
00:04:31,937 --> 00:04:34,687
Kikuoka: YOU’RE RIGHT,
AND, UNTIL NOW, IT WAS.

83
00:04:34,687 --> 00:04:38,397
BUT WITH THE SOUL TRANSLATOR,
WE CAN SCAN A HUMAN SOUL,

84
00:04:38,397 --> 00:04:41,027
OR SPECIFICALLY
THE QUANTUM FIELD IN BRAIN CELLS

85
00:04:41,027 --> 00:04:42,857
WE CALL THE FLUCTLIGHT.

86
00:04:42,857 --> 00:04:44,737
Higa: IF YOU’RE WONDERING
WHERE WE’RE GONNA PUT

87
00:04:44,737 --> 00:04:47,867
ALL THE DATA OF A HUMAN BRAIN,
STOP WONDERING.

88
00:04:47,867 --> 00:04:50,077
WE MADE THE LIGHT
QUANTUM GATE CRYSTAL,

89
00:04:50,077 --> 00:04:53,037
OR LIGHTCUBE, TO STORE
ALL THAT GOOD STUFF ON.

90
00:04:53,037 --> 00:04:55,167
Rinko: THEORETICALLY,
YOU COULD SAVE

91
00:04:55,167 --> 00:04:56,997
A ONE-TO-ONE COPY
OF A FLUCTLIGHT.

92
00:04:56,997 --> 00:04:58,957
Kikuoka: THAT’S CORRECT,

93
00:04:58,957 --> 00:05:01,217
ALTHOUGH IT’S NOT A THEORY.

94
00:05:01,217 --> 00:05:03,757
WE’VE ALREADY COPIED
A HUMAN SOUL.

95
00:05:03,757 --> 00:05:05,087
( both gasp )

96
00:05:05,087 --> 00:05:06,967
Rinko: BUT THEN,
WHY’D YOU BOTHER

97
00:05:06,967 --> 00:05:08,597
ASKING ME TO COME HELP YOU?

98
00:05:08,597 --> 00:05:12,437
Kikuoka: BECAUSE, LIKE IDIOTS,
WE MISSED SOMETHING.

99
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:14,347
THE HUMAN SOUL IS COMPLEX.

100
00:05:14,347 --> 00:05:16,227
SURE, WE CAN COPY IT,

101
00:05:16,227 --> 00:05:19,567
BUT THERE’S A WIDE GAP
BETWEEN IT AND A TRUE A.I.

102
00:05:19,567 --> 00:05:20,777
- HIGA.
- Higa: EH?

103
00:05:20,777 --> 00:05:22,947
Kikuoka: GO ON.

104
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:24,657
SHOW OUR GUESTS A DEMONSTRATION.

105
00:05:24,657 --> 00:05:26,657
Higa: DAMN. YOU’RE SADISTIC.

106
00:05:26,657 --> 00:05:28,487
( sighs )

107
00:05:33,457 --> 00:05:34,827
Male: IS THE SAMPLING DONE YET?

108
00:05:34,827 --> 00:05:38,167
Higa: YUP. NO PROBLEMS.
LOOKING GOOD.

109
00:05:38,167 --> 00:05:42,837
Male: SWEET! SO WHY’S IT DARK,
AND HOW COME I CAN’T MOVE?

110
00:05:42,837 --> 00:05:44,547
OH, I KNOW WHY.

111
00:05:44,547 --> 00:05:46,637
LET ME OUT.
THE S.T.L.’s GLITCHIN’.

112
00:05:46,637 --> 00:05:49,097
Higa: SORRY, BUDDY.
I CAN’T LOG YOU OUT.

113
00:05:49,097 --> 00:05:50,967
Male: DUDE, WHAT THE HELL?

114
00:05:50,967 --> 00:05:52,637
LET ME OUT OF HERE!

115
00:05:52,637 --> 00:05:54,727
WHO ARE YOU?!
I DON’T RECOGNIZE YOUR VOICE!

116
00:05:54,727 --> 00:05:57,397
Higa: TAKERU HIGA.
YOU KNOW THAT.

117
00:05:59,687 --> 00:06:02,487
Male: WHAT?! NO WAY! I’M HIGA!

118
00:06:02,487 --> 00:06:03,737
LET ME OUT, AND YOU’LL SEE!

119
00:06:03,737 --> 00:06:05,067
Higa: RELAX.

120
00:06:05,067 --> 00:06:07,947
YOU’RE TAKERU HIGA, THE COPY.

121
00:06:07,947 --> 00:06:09,617
I KNOW YOU KNOW
WHAT’S GOING ON,

122
00:06:09,617 --> 00:06:10,947
SO JUST ACCEPT
THE SITUATION AN--

123
00:06:10,947 --> 00:06:13,657
Higa copy: SCREW YOU! I’M ME!

124
00:06:13,657 --> 00:06:15,917
IF I’M A COPY,
THEN I’D KNOW IT, GOD DAMN IT!

125
00:06:15,917 --> 00:06:17,787
COME ON! PLEASE!

126
00:06:17,787 --> 00:06:20,707
LET ME OUT,
YOU SON OF A BITCH, RIGHT NOW!

127
00:06:20,707 --> 00:06:22,337
Kikuoka: WE TALKED ABOUT THIS.

128
00:06:22,337 --> 00:06:24,627
YOU NEED TO CALM DOWN.
IF YOU CAN’T THINK RATIONALLY,

129
00:06:24,627 --> 00:06:26,047
YOUR FLUCTLIGHT WON’T BE ABLE
TO TAKE THE STRAIN.

130
00:06:26,047 --> 00:06:27,757
Higa copy: I AM RATIONAL!

131
00:06:27,757 --> 00:06:30,927
OKAY, THEN! LET’S SEE
WHO’S FASTER AT PI,

132
00:06:30,927 --> 00:06:31,847
ME OR THAT FAKER!

133
00:06:31,847 --> 00:06:35,137
3.141592653589793...

134
00:06:35,137 --> 00:06:37,687
( accelerated speech, static )

135
00:06:41,767 --> 00:06:43,817
( Higa sighs )

136
00:06:43,817 --> 00:06:47,067
FULL COLLAPSE,
ONE MINUTE, EIGHT SECONDS.

137
00:06:47,067 --> 00:06:48,947
( Asuna gags )

138
00:06:48,947 --> 00:06:50,657
Rinko: ALL RIGHT,
THAT WAS BEYOND TWISTED!

139
00:06:50,657 --> 00:06:52,577
Kikuoka: IT IS DISTURBING.

140
00:06:52,577 --> 00:06:54,697
STILL, IT’S THE BEST WAY
TO EXPLAIN

141
00:06:54,697 --> 00:06:57,157
WHAT WE’VE BEEN ABLE
TO ACCOMPLISH UP TO NOW.

142
00:06:57,157 --> 00:06:58,617
I’M SORRY YOU HAD TO SEE IT.

143
00:06:58,617 --> 00:07:01,837
WE COPIED OVER A DOZEN
FLUCTLIGHTS, INCLUDING MINE,

144
00:07:01,837 --> 00:07:03,957
AND SUBMITTED THEM
TO THE SAME TEST.

145
00:07:03,957 --> 00:07:05,757
THE RESULTS
WERE ALWAYS THE SAME.

146
00:07:05,757 --> 00:07:08,467
THEIR LOGIC SYSTEMS WENT
HAYWIRE, AND THEY COLLAPSED.

147
00:07:08,467 --> 00:07:11,137
SINCE MATURE FLUCTLIGHTS
DON’T WORK,

148
00:07:11,137 --> 00:07:12,387
WHAT WOULD YOU TRY NEXT?

149
00:07:12,387 --> 00:07:14,887
Rinko: MAYBE WIPE
THEIR MEMORIES.

150
00:07:14,887 --> 00:07:17,097
OR RAISE A SOUL FROM SCRATCH.

151
00:07:17,097 --> 00:07:18,097
Asuna: YOU DIDN’T.

152
00:07:18,097 --> 00:07:20,097
Kikuoka: YES, WE DID.

153
00:07:20,097 --> 00:07:23,817
WE PUT NEWBORNS INTO THE S.T.L.
AND COPIED THEIR SOULS.

154
00:07:23,817 --> 00:07:25,107
( both gasp )

155
00:07:25,107 --> 00:07:26,777
Rinko: THESE COPIES
ARE ESSENTIALLY HUMAN,

156
00:07:26,777 --> 00:07:29,447
SO HOW WOULD YOU RAISE THEM?
NOT IN A VOID.

157
00:07:29,447 --> 00:07:31,777
YOU’D NEED AN EXACT COPY
OF THE REAL WORLD.

158
00:07:31,777 --> 00:07:34,367
Kikuoka: THAT’S IMPOSSIBLE.
WE CAN’T DO THAT YET,

159
00:07:34,367 --> 00:07:37,117
SO WE WENT LOOKING
FOR AN ALTERNATIVE,

160
00:07:37,117 --> 00:07:39,577
AND WE FOUND IT ONLINE.

161
00:07:39,577 --> 00:07:42,037
Asuna: V.R.M.M.O. WORLDS.

162
00:07:42,037 --> 00:07:43,287
Higa: DANG, YOU’RE SHARP.

163
00:07:43,287 --> 00:07:46,007
USING THE SEED,
WE MADE OUR OWN WORLD,

164
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:48,467
WITH VILLAGES AND TERRAIN,
AND CONVERTED IT

165
00:07:48,467 --> 00:07:51,007
TO MNEMONIC VISUALS
FOR THE S.T.L.

166
00:07:51,007 --> 00:07:52,677
Kikuoka: WE PLACED
FOUR OF OUR STAFF

167
00:07:52,677 --> 00:07:54,467
IN THE FIRST VILLAGE WE CREATED.

168
00:07:54,467 --> 00:07:56,927
THEY ACTED AS PARENTS
TO 16 A.I. INFANTS,

169
00:07:56,927 --> 00:07:58,597
OR SOUL ARCHETYPES,

170
00:07:58,597 --> 00:08:00,437
AND RAISED THEM
’TIL THEY WERE 18.

171
00:08:01,847 --> 00:08:04,607
WE MONITORED THE YOUNGSTERS
AS THEY GREW UP.

172
00:08:04,607 --> 00:08:06,027
OH, BY THE WAY,

173
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:08,607
OFFICIALLY, WE CALL THEM
ARTIFICIAL FLUCTLIGHTS.

174
00:08:08,607 --> 00:08:10,817
ANYWAY, WE WERE
MORE THAN SATISFIED

175
00:08:10,817 --> 00:08:12,407
WITH HOW THEY TURNED OUT.

176
00:08:12,407 --> 00:08:15,027
THEY WERE SHARP,
OBEDIENT, AND UPSTANDING.

177
00:08:15,027 --> 00:08:18,827
WHEN THEY EVENTUALLY PAIRED UP,
WE MADE THEM PARENTS

178
00:08:18,827 --> 00:08:21,997
AND GAVE THEM
NEW SOUL ARCHETYPES TO RAISE.

179
00:08:21,997 --> 00:08:23,127
OUR STAFF WAS OUT BY THEN,

180
00:08:23,127 --> 00:08:25,587
SO WE ACCELERATED TIME
BY 5,000,

181
00:08:25,587 --> 00:08:28,547
AND SOON WE HAD
MULTIPLE GENERATIONS.

182
00:08:28,547 --> 00:08:31,087
AFTER THREE WEEKS
HAD PASSED IN OUR WORLD,

183
00:08:31,087 --> 00:08:33,297
300 HAD PASSED IN THEIRS.

184
00:08:33,297 --> 00:08:35,807
NOW THEY HAVE
A FULLY FUNCTIONING SOCIETY

185
00:08:35,807 --> 00:08:38,017
WITH A POPULATION OF 80,000.

186
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:41,557
Rinko: YOU SIMULATED
AN ENTIRE CIVILIZATION.

187
00:08:41,557 --> 00:08:42,807
Kikuoka: EXACTLY.

188
00:08:42,807 --> 00:08:45,897
SO FAR, 480 YEARS
HAVE PASSED THERE.

189
00:08:45,897 --> 00:08:47,317
THE CAPITAL, CENTORIA,

190
00:08:47,317 --> 00:08:49,647
HAS 20,000 CITIZENS
LIVING IN IT.

191
00:08:49,647 --> 00:08:51,987
Higa: AT THIS POINT,
ALL THE A.I. FLUCTLIGHTS

192
00:08:51,987 --> 00:08:53,987
HAVE MATURED
INTO THE BOTTOM-UP A.I.s

193
00:08:53,987 --> 00:08:55,157
WE WERE SHOOTING FOR.

194
00:08:55,157 --> 00:08:57,487
WE WERE ALL READY
TO HIT THE NEXT PHASE

195
00:08:57,487 --> 00:09:00,077
AND WERE STOKED ABOUT IT,
BUT THEN...

196
00:09:00,077 --> 00:09:02,157
Kikuoka: WE NOTICED
A MAJOR ISSUE

197
00:09:02,157 --> 00:09:03,247
WHICH STOOD IN OUR WAY.

198
00:09:03,247 --> 00:09:05,207
Rinko: WHAT ISSUE?

199
00:09:05,207 --> 00:09:06,207
Kikuoka:
THE GOVERNING BODY THERE,

200
00:09:06,207 --> 00:09:07,917
CALLED THE AXIOM CHURCH,

201
00:09:07,917 --> 00:09:10,667
CREATED A SET OF LAWS
CALLED THE TABOO INDEX.

202
00:09:10,667 --> 00:09:12,377
Asuna: THE WHAT INDEX?

203
00:09:12,377 --> 00:09:15,087
Kikuoka: THE TABOO INDEX.
IT CONTAINS LAWS

204
00:09:15,087 --> 00:09:17,887
LIKE ONE FORBIDDING MURDER,
JUST LIKE WE HAVE.

205
00:09:17,887 --> 00:09:19,927
AND, IF YOU’VE BEEN
WATCHING THE NEWS RECENTLY,

206
00:09:19,927 --> 00:09:23,057
YOU CAN SEE HOW DIFFICULT
THAT ONE IS FOR HUMANS TO OBEY,

207
00:09:23,057 --> 00:09:25,857
BUT THE FLUCTLIGHTS OBEY
ALL THEIR LAWS TO THE LETTER.

208
00:09:25,857 --> 00:09:28,567
THEY’RE OBSESSIVE ABOUT IT.

209
00:09:28,567 --> 00:09:32,447
THIS TOWN IS BEAUTIFUL,
BUT TOO PERFECT.

210
00:09:32,447 --> 00:09:33,897
THERE’S NO LITTER
ON THE STREETS

211
00:09:33,897 --> 00:09:35,277
AND NO CRIME TO SPEAK OF.

212
00:09:35,277 --> 00:09:37,277
NEEDLESS TO SAY,
THERE’S NOT BEEN

213
00:09:37,277 --> 00:09:39,987
A SINGLE MURDER
COMMITTED HERE, EITHER.

214
00:09:39,987 --> 00:09:43,617
Rinko: AND THAT WOULD BE
A GOOD THING, WOULDN’T IT?

215
00:09:43,617 --> 00:09:46,787
Asuna: IT WOULDN’T,
NOT FOR HIM, ANYWAY.

216
00:09:46,787 --> 00:09:48,997
HE WANTS A.I.s THAT CAN KILL.

217
00:09:48,997 --> 00:09:50,957
( Rinko gasps )

218
00:09:50,957 --> 00:09:53,467
Asuna: KIRITO AND I WERE WRONG.
WE THOUGHT WE KNEW

219
00:09:53,467 --> 00:09:56,837
WHY YOU WERE INTERESTED
IN V.R.M.M.O.s, FOR TRAINING.

220
00:09:56,837 --> 00:09:58,757
WE FIGURED
YOU’D USE THE TECHNOLOGY

221
00:09:58,757 --> 00:10:00,927
TO TRAIN SOLDIERS AND POLICE.

222
00:10:00,927 --> 00:10:03,847
BUT FOR AN OFFICER OF THE S.D.F.

223
00:10:03,847 --> 00:10:06,057
TO ATTEMPT
SOMETHING ON THIS SCALE,

224
00:10:06,057 --> 00:10:07,977
THERE HAS TO BE MORE AT STAKE,

225
00:10:07,977 --> 00:10:09,767
AND THERE IS.

226
00:10:09,767 --> 00:10:13,067
THIS PROJECT IS ABOUT
CREATING A.I. FOR WARFARE,

227
00:10:13,067 --> 00:10:14,147
ISN’T IT?

228
00:10:15,777 --> 00:10:18,567
Rinko: IS THAT TRUE, KIKUOKA?

229
00:10:20,367 --> 00:10:22,157
Kikuoka: FIVE YEARS AGO,

230
00:10:22,157 --> 00:10:26,117
WHEN THE NERVEGEAR WAS
FIRST ANNOUNCED, I HAD AN IDEA.

231
00:10:26,117 --> 00:10:29,127
ALTHOUGH IT WAS MEANT
FOR GAMING, THIS NEW TECHNOLOGY

232
00:10:29,127 --> 00:10:32,337
HAD THE POTENTIAL
TO CHANGE HOW WARS WERE FOUGHT.

233
00:10:32,337 --> 00:10:34,967
WHEN THE "S.A.O."
INCIDENT HAPPENED,

234
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:37,377
I ASKED TO BE TRANSFERRED
TO THE MINISTRY,

235
00:10:37,377 --> 00:10:39,597
THEN JOINED
THE TASK FORCE THERE.

236
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:44,097
THAT WAS ALL SO I COULD GET
THIS PROJECT OFF THE GROUND,

237
00:10:44,097 --> 00:10:47,807
AND FIVE YEARS LATER,
HERE WE ARE.

238
00:10:47,807 --> 00:10:49,227
Rinko: THAT’S HIS REASON,

239
00:10:49,227 --> 00:10:51,937
BUT WHY DID YOU DECIDE
TO TAKE PART IN THIS?

240
00:10:51,937 --> 00:10:54,527
Higa: OH. UM,
THAT’S A WHOLE ’NOTHER STORY.

241
00:10:54,527 --> 00:10:57,487
FOR ME, IT’S PERSONAL.
WHEN I WAS IN COLLEGE,

242
00:10:57,487 --> 00:10:59,907
I HAD A BUD IN KOREA
WHO WAS IN THE ARMY THERE.

243
00:10:59,907 --> 00:11:02,367
THEN HE GOT KILLED
ON ONE OF HIS TOURS.

244
00:11:02,367 --> 00:11:05,447
SO I THOUGHT THIS STUPID WORLD

245
00:11:05,447 --> 00:11:08,037
AIN’T GONNA STOP
HAVIN’ WARS ANYTIME SOON.

246
00:11:08,037 --> 00:11:10,077
BUT IF WE COULD FIGURE OUT
HOW TO HAVE ’EM

247
00:11:10,077 --> 00:11:12,337
WITHOUT KILLING PEOPLE, THEN...

248
00:11:12,337 --> 00:11:14,587
( chuckles )
SOUNDS NAÏVE, RIGHT?

249
00:11:14,587 --> 00:11:16,967
Asuna: YOU DIDN’T
TELL KIRITO ANY OF THIS

250
00:11:16,967 --> 00:11:19,087
BEFORE YOU HIRED HIM, DID YOU?

251
00:11:19,087 --> 00:11:20,887
Kikuoka: WOULD IT
MATTER IF I DID?

252
00:11:20,887 --> 00:11:22,637
Asuna: YES, IT WOULD HAVE.

253
00:11:22,637 --> 00:11:26,097
IF YOU HAD TOLD HIM, HE NEVER
WOULD HAVE AGREED TO HELP.

254
00:11:26,097 --> 00:11:29,437
THERE’S ONE IMPORTANT ISSUE
YOUR PLAN DOESN’T EVEN ADDRESS.

255
00:11:29,437 --> 00:11:30,727
Kikuoka: WHICH IS?

256
00:11:30,727 --> 00:11:33,397
Asuna: THE RIGHTS OF THE A.I.s.

257
00:11:33,397 --> 00:11:36,857
THESE THINGS YOU CALL
ARTIFICIAL FLUCTLIGHTS,

258
00:11:36,857 --> 00:11:39,487
THEY’RE STILL MENTALLY
AND EMOTIONALLY HUMAN.

259
00:11:39,487 --> 00:11:42,367
Kikuoka: TRUE, BUT IT’S NOT
LIKE THEY HAVE PHYSICAL BODIES.

260
00:11:42,367 --> 00:11:45,407
Asuna: BUT OTHERWISE,
THEY’RE NO DIFFERENT FROM US,

261
00:11:45,407 --> 00:11:48,077
AND YOU’RE FORCING THEM
TO BE YOUR TOOLS OF WAR.

262
00:11:48,077 --> 00:11:52,207
KIRITO WOULD NEVER
AGREE TO THAT, EVER.

263
00:11:52,207 --> 00:11:53,497
Kikuoka: LOOK, I UNDERSTAND

264
00:11:53,497 --> 00:11:55,297
THE POINT YOU’RE
TRYING TO MAKE HERE.

265
00:11:55,297 --> 00:11:59,047
BUT, TO ME,
THE LIFE OF ONE S.D.F. SOLDIER

266
00:11:59,047 --> 00:12:01,507
IS WORTH FAR MORE
THAN 100,000 A.I.s.

267
00:12:05,387 --> 00:12:08,887
Rinko: ANYWAY, WHY DID YOU
NEED KIRIGAYA FOR THIS?

268
00:12:08,887 --> 00:12:11,517
I CAN’T UNDERSTAND
WHY YOU’D USE A CIVILIAN

269
00:12:11,517 --> 00:12:13,397
ON A PROJECT
THAT’S SO CONFIDENTIAL.

270
00:12:13,397 --> 00:12:16,437
Kikuoka: I’M SORRY.
I GOT SO CARRIED AWAY

271
00:12:16,437 --> 00:12:18,857
TALKING ABOUT THE PROJECT,
I ALMOST FORGOT.

272
00:12:18,857 --> 00:12:21,737
WE NEEDED TO KNOW
WHY THE A.I. FLUCTLIGHTS

273
00:12:21,737 --> 00:12:24,067
COULDN’T DISOBEY
THE TABOO INDEX,

274
00:12:24,067 --> 00:12:27,117
SO I CAME UP
WITH AN EXPERIMENT.

275
00:12:27,117 --> 00:12:29,367
IF WE BLOCKED
A HUMAN’S MEMORIES,

276
00:12:29,367 --> 00:12:30,957
REVERTED HIM TO CHILDHOOD,

277
00:12:30,957 --> 00:12:33,747
AND HAD HIM GROW UP
IN OUR V.R. WORLD,

278
00:12:33,747 --> 00:12:36,667
WOULD HE BE ABLE
TO DISOBEY THE TABOO INDEX?

279
00:12:38,087 --> 00:12:39,207
TO CARRY THIS OUT,

280
00:12:39,207 --> 00:12:40,717
WE NEEDED SOMEONE
WITH EXPERIENCE

281
00:12:40,717 --> 00:12:42,717
NAVIGATING
IN A V.R. ENVIRONMENT,

282
00:12:42,717 --> 00:12:45,387
NOT JUST A WEEK OR
A MONTH’S WORTH OF EXPERIENCE.

283
00:12:45,387 --> 00:12:46,347
I’M TALKING YEARS.

284
00:12:46,347 --> 00:12:47,257
( Asuna gasps )

285
00:12:49,477 --> 00:12:51,227
Kikuoka:
THAT’S WHY I NEEDED HIM.

286
00:12:53,687 --> 00:12:55,187
Leafa: I CAN’T BELIEVE KAZUTO

287
00:12:55,187 --> 00:12:57,937
WOULD SIGN UP
FOR SOMETHING LIKE THAT.

288
00:12:57,937 --> 00:12:59,817
( Silica sighs )
CAN WE EVEN TRUST

289
00:12:59,817 --> 00:13:01,897
ANYTHING KIKUOKA SAYS ANYMORE?

290
00:13:01,897 --> 00:13:03,317
Lisbeth: I BET HE ONLY TOLD YOU

291
00:13:03,317 --> 00:13:05,407
A FRACTION
OF WHAT HE’S REALLY UP TO.

292
00:13:05,407 --> 00:13:07,277
Sinon: I GUESS ALL WE CAN DO NOW

293
00:13:07,277 --> 00:13:10,157
IS HOPE THE TREATMENT KIRITO
GETS IN THE S.T.L. WILL WORK.

294
00:13:10,157 --> 00:13:12,117
( Silica sighs )

295
00:13:12,117 --> 00:13:14,287
Lisbeth: WHAT HAPPENED
WITH THAT TABOO INDEX THING,

296
00:13:14,287 --> 00:13:15,877
YOU KNOW, THE EXPERIMENT?

297
00:13:15,877 --> 00:13:17,247
DID HE TELL YOU IF IT WORKED?

298
00:13:17,247 --> 00:13:20,047
Asuna: MM-HMM.
KIRITO GOT TO BE CLOSE FRIENDS

299
00:13:20,047 --> 00:13:22,217
WITH TWO OTHERS,
A BOY AND A GIRL.

300
00:13:22,217 --> 00:13:26,257
KIKUOKA SAID THE GIRL ENDED UP
BREAKING ONE OF THE LAWS.

301
00:13:26,257 --> 00:13:29,137
Sinon: REALLY?
DID SHE DO IT BECAUSE OF KIRITO?

302
00:13:29,137 --> 00:13:30,557
Asuna: UH-HUH.

303
00:13:30,557 --> 00:13:32,977
APPARENTLY, SHE VIOLATED A TABOO

304
00:13:32,977 --> 00:13:36,477
BY TRYING TO ACCESS
A RESTRICTED ADDRESS.

305
00:13:36,477 --> 00:13:38,147
Higa: ACCORDING TO THE LOG,

306
00:13:38,147 --> 00:13:40,357
THE GIRL SAW
ANOTHER A.I. FLUCTLIGHT

307
00:13:40,357 --> 00:13:42,107
DIE IN THE RESTRICTED AREA,

308
00:13:42,107 --> 00:13:45,567
AND, FROM WHAT WE CAN TELL,
SHE WAS TRYING TO SAVE HIM.

309
00:13:45,567 --> 00:13:48,407
Kikuoka: SHE HAD MORE CONCERN
FOR ANOTHER PERSON’S LIFE

310
00:13:48,407 --> 00:13:51,197
THAN SHE HAD
FOR DISOBEYING THE TABOO INDEX.

311
00:13:51,197 --> 00:13:54,287
SHE CHOSE TO DO IT, AND THAT’S
WHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR.

312
00:13:54,287 --> 00:13:56,997
( girls grumble )

313
00:13:56,997 --> 00:13:58,787
Silica: THAT’S KIND OF
A NEAT STORY.

314
00:13:58,787 --> 00:14:01,007
Lisbeth: YEAH, IF ONLY IT WASN’T

315
00:14:01,007 --> 00:14:03,257
ABOUT TRAINING A.I.s
TO KILL PEOPLE.

316
00:14:03,257 --> 00:14:06,637
Asuna: YOU’RE RIGHT.
BUT LOOK AT WHAT SHE DID.

317
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:10,467
SHE WENT AGAINST THE SYSTEM
JUST TO HELP SOMEONE ELSE.

318
00:14:10,467 --> 00:14:12,217
Leafa: DOES THIS
A.I. GIRL HAVE A NAME?

319
00:14:12,217 --> 00:14:13,137
Asuna: YES.

320
00:14:16,017 --> 00:14:17,017
ALICE?

321
00:14:17,017 --> 00:14:18,357
Kikuoka: THAT’S RIGHT.

322
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:20,767
I WAS STUNNED
WHEN I FOUND OUT.

323
00:14:20,767 --> 00:14:24,107
HER HAVING THAT NAME
IS QUITE THE COINCIDENCE.

324
00:14:24,107 --> 00:14:25,527
THE NAME ALICE, YOU SEE,

325
00:14:25,527 --> 00:14:28,117
ALSO HAPPENS TO BE
THE NAME OF THE CONCEPT

326
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:30,527
THAT WAS THE FOUNDATION
FOR RATH AND THIS PROJECT.

327
00:14:30,527 --> 00:14:32,747
Asuna: CONCEPT?

328
00:14:32,747 --> 00:14:36,207
Kikuoka: AN A.I. THAT IS
HIGHLY ADAPTIVE AND AUTONOMOUS,

329
00:14:36,207 --> 00:14:38,917
MORE SPECIFICALLY,
AN ARTIFICIAL

330
00:14:38,917 --> 00:14:42,247
LABILE INTELLIGENCE
CYBERNATED EXISTENCE,

331
00:14:42,247 --> 00:14:44,417
OR THE ACRONYM "ALICE."

332
00:14:44,417 --> 00:14:46,507
OUR GOAL ULTIMATELY

333
00:14:46,507 --> 00:14:49,337
WAS TO TURN AN A.I. FLUCTLIGHT
INTO AN ALICE.

334
00:14:51,807 --> 00:14:56,477
THEREFORE, WE CALLED IT
PROJECT ALICIZATION.

335
00:14:58,307 --> 00:15:00,437
Leafa: THAT SOUNDS
SO COMPLICATED.

336
00:15:00,437 --> 00:15:03,477
Asuna: YEAH. I DON’T UNDERSTAND
A LOT OF WHAT HE SAID, EITHER.

337
00:15:03,477 --> 00:15:06,487
BUT HE SAID IF THEY
HAD SAVED ALICE’S FLUCTLIGHT,

338
00:15:06,487 --> 00:15:09,447
THEIR RESEARCH WOULD BE
MUCH FURTHER ALONG BY NOW.

339
00:15:09,447 --> 00:15:10,987
Lisbeth: MM. DID SHE DIE?

340
00:15:10,987 --> 00:15:13,237
Asuna: NO, SHE’S STILL ALIVE,

341
00:15:13,237 --> 00:15:15,947
BUT REMEMBER I SAID
TIME THERE’S FASTER THAN HERE?

342
00:15:15,947 --> 00:15:17,157
Lisbeth: MM-HMM.

343
00:15:17,157 --> 00:15:19,287
Asuna: WELL,
BY THE TIME THEY NOTICED,

344
00:15:19,287 --> 00:15:21,207
TWO DAYS HAD GONE BY THERE.

345
00:15:21,207 --> 00:15:23,247
SHE WAS TAKEN TO THE CAPITAL,

346
00:15:23,247 --> 00:15:25,627
AND THE AXIOM CHURCH
HAD HER FLUCTLIGHT ALTERED.

347
00:15:25,627 --> 00:15:27,417
Sinon: THEY CHANGED HER SOUL?

348
00:15:27,417 --> 00:15:29,427
HOW COULD THEY
GIVE A.I. FLUCTLIGHTS

349
00:15:29,427 --> 00:15:31,347
THAT KIND OF AUTHORITY
OVER EACH OTHER?

350
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:34,217
Asuna: THEY DON’T
REALLY KNOW HOW IT HAPPENED,

351
00:15:34,217 --> 00:15:36,977
BUT THEY THINK IT MIGHT BE
A SYSTEM EXPLOIT.

352
00:15:36,977 --> 00:15:38,767
A FEW OF THE A.I. FLUCTLIGHTS

353
00:15:38,767 --> 00:15:41,267
CAN USE
WHAT THEY CALL "SACRED ARTS."

354
00:15:41,267 --> 00:15:42,687
THEY’RE BASICALLY
SYSTEM ACCESS AUTHORITIES

355
00:15:42,687 --> 00:15:44,687
THAT LOOK LIKE MAGIC SPELLS.

356
00:15:44,687 --> 00:15:46,397
( gasps ) SORRY.

357
00:15:46,397 --> 00:15:48,107
I HAVE TO LOG OUT NOW.

358
00:15:48,107 --> 00:15:50,487
Leafa: WHY? WHAT’S THE RUSH?

359
00:15:50,487 --> 00:15:53,367
Asuna: THEY SAID THEY’D LET ME
LOOK IN ON KIRITO FOR A BIT.

360
00:15:53,367 --> 00:15:55,237
I DON’T WANT
TO BE LATE FOR THAT.

361
00:15:55,237 --> 00:15:56,577
Lisbeth: YOU GET
TO WATCH HIM SLEEP.

362
00:15:56,577 --> 00:15:57,577
TELL US IF HE DROOLS.

363
00:15:57,577 --> 00:15:59,207
( Asuna laughs )

364
00:15:59,207 --> 00:16:01,127
I DON’T THINK I’LL SEE HIS FACE.

365
00:16:01,127 --> 00:16:03,287
THE MACHINE HE’S IN
COVERS IT UP.

366
00:16:03,287 --> 00:16:05,207
♪

367
00:16:11,427 --> 00:16:12,337
Rinko: EH?

368
00:16:13,427 --> 00:16:15,597
NUMBER FOUR...

369
00:16:15,597 --> 00:16:17,847
AND THAT’S FIVE.

370
00:16:17,847 --> 00:16:19,637
Aki: THEY’RE STILL
BUILDING UNIT SIX.

371
00:16:19,637 --> 00:16:22,347
IT’S IN ROPPONGI
WITH UNIT ONE, THE PROTOTYPE.

372
00:16:22,347 --> 00:16:24,767
TWO AND THREE ARE HERE.

373
00:16:24,767 --> 00:16:27,357
WELL, ACTUALLY THEY’RE
IN THE LOWER SHAFT.

374
00:16:27,357 --> 00:16:29,317
- Asuna: MS. AKI.
- ( Aki chuckles )

375
00:16:29,317 --> 00:16:30,817
Asuna: WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

376
00:16:30,817 --> 00:16:33,527
Aki: I’M TAKING CARE
OF KIRIGAYA.

377
00:16:33,527 --> 00:16:36,447
Asuna: BUT YOU WERE HIS NURSE
AT THAT HOSPITAL IN CHIYODA.

378
00:16:36,447 --> 00:16:38,077
( gasps ) WAIT.

379
00:16:38,077 --> 00:16:40,997
ARE YOU A NURSE,
OR ARE YOU JUST FAKING?!

380
00:16:40,997 --> 00:16:43,577
Aki: I’M A NURSE.
I’M REGISTERED AND EVERYTHING

381
00:16:43,577 --> 00:16:45,417
AND HAVE
THE PAPERS TO PROVE IT.

382
00:16:45,417 --> 00:16:47,337
ALTHOUGH, FULL DISCLOSURE,

383
00:16:47,337 --> 00:16:49,507
THE NURSING SCHOOL
I GRADUATED FROM

384
00:16:49,507 --> 00:16:51,467
IS AFFILIATED WITH
THE TOKYO SELF-DEFENSE FORCE.

385
00:16:51,467 --> 00:16:52,927
( Asuna gasps )

386
00:16:52,927 --> 00:16:55,677
Aki: SERGEANT FIRST CLASS
NATSUKI AKI.

387
00:16:55,677 --> 00:16:59,387
AS LONG AS I’M ON DUTY HERE,
I SWEAR I WILL PROTECT KIRIGAYA.

388
00:16:59,387 --> 00:17:00,307
WE GOOD?

389
00:17:02,727 --> 00:17:05,607
( Asuna sighs )
YEAH. WE’RE GOOD.

390
00:17:05,607 --> 00:17:07,647
Aki: DON’T YOU WORRY
ABOUT A THING.

391
00:17:07,647 --> 00:17:09,567
♪

392
00:17:12,067 --> 00:17:15,567
Asuna: IN YOUR OPINION,
WILL HE BE OKAY?

393
00:17:15,567 --> 00:17:17,237
Aki: OF COURSE HE WILL.

394
00:17:17,237 --> 00:17:18,827
HIS FLUCTLIGHT’S STABLE SO FAR,

395
00:17:18,827 --> 00:17:20,827
AND HIS NEURAL NETWORK’S
ON THE MEND.

396
00:17:20,827 --> 00:17:22,747
ALL HIS VITALS
ARE LOOKING GOOD, TOO.

397
00:17:22,747 --> 00:17:24,497
HE IS A TOUGH COOKIE.

398
00:17:24,497 --> 00:17:26,877
HE’S THE ONE
WHO CLEARED "S.A.O.," AFTER ALL.

399
00:17:34,337 --> 00:17:35,217
( Rinko sighs )

400
00:17:37,347 --> 00:17:38,347
CAN WE TALK?

401
00:17:38,347 --> 00:17:39,677
Asuna: EH? HUH?

402
00:17:41,347 --> 00:17:42,477
Rinko: THERE’S...

403
00:17:42,477 --> 00:17:45,517
SOMETHING I HAVE
TO CONFESS TO YOU.

404
00:17:45,517 --> 00:17:48,477
MM-MMM. NOT JUST TO YOU.

405
00:17:48,477 --> 00:17:51,487
I OWE ONE
TO ALL THE "S.A.O." PLAYERS,

406
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:53,197
LIVING AND DEAD.

407
00:17:53,197 --> 00:17:54,447
( Asuna sighs )

408
00:17:54,447 --> 00:17:56,317
Rinko: I’M SURE
YOU HEARD THE STORY

409
00:17:56,317 --> 00:17:58,577
ABOUT HOW,
DURING THE "S.A.O." INCIDENT,

410
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:02,077
AKIHIKO KAYABA AND I WERE HIDING
IN THE MOUNTAINS OF NAGANO?

411
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:07,457
THAT SCAR’S FROM A MICRO-BOMB
AKIHIKO IMPLANTED THERE.

412
00:18:07,457 --> 00:18:09,167
( Asuna gasps )

413
00:18:09,167 --> 00:18:10,957
Rinko: THE NEWS
SAID HE PUT IT THERE

414
00:18:10,957 --> 00:18:13,167
TO FORCE ME TO STAY
AND HELP HIM WITH HIS PLAN

415
00:18:13,167 --> 00:18:15,677
DURING THOSE TWO YEARS,

416
00:18:15,677 --> 00:18:17,337
BUT THAT’S NOT THE TRUTH.

417
00:18:17,337 --> 00:18:19,597
YES, THE BOMB WAS REAL,

418
00:18:19,597 --> 00:18:22,427
BUT I KNEW
IT WOULD NEVER GO OFF.

419
00:18:22,427 --> 00:18:24,637
HE PUT IT THERE
SO THAT, WHEN WE WERE CAUGHT,

420
00:18:24,637 --> 00:18:26,977
I WOULDN’T BE CHARGED
WITH AIDING AND ABETTING.

421
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:30,567
IT WAS A BLUFF TO KEEP ME SAFE

422
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:33,607
AND THE ONLY PRESENT
HE EVER GAVE ME.

423
00:18:33,607 --> 00:18:37,487
WHEN AKIHIKO GOT INTO THE TOTO
INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY,

424
00:18:37,487 --> 00:18:40,157
HE WAS ALREADY
HEAD OF DEVELOPMENT AT ARGUS,

425
00:18:40,157 --> 00:18:42,787
BUT I DIDN’T KNOW ABOUT THAT.

426
00:18:42,787 --> 00:18:44,907
ALL I SAW WAS A SCRAWNY LONER

427
00:18:44,907 --> 00:18:46,707
WHO ONLY CARED
ABOUT HIS RESEARCH.

428
00:18:51,587 --> 00:18:54,167
YOU WANT SOME INSPIRATION?

429
00:18:54,167 --> 00:18:56,297
THEN GET OUT ONCE IN A WHILE!

430
00:18:56,297 --> 00:18:57,627
( Kayaba stammers )

431
00:18:58,717 --> 00:19:00,347
I NEED TO FIND A WAY

432
00:19:00,347 --> 00:19:03,517
TO EMULATE THE FEELING
OF SUNLIGHT ON THE SKIN.

433
00:19:03,517 --> 00:19:04,727
Rinko: WHAT?

434
00:19:04,727 --> 00:19:06,887
WE WERE TOTAL OPPOSITES,

435
00:19:06,887 --> 00:19:08,227
BUT WE STARTED DATING.

436
00:19:10,267 --> 00:19:11,397
( no audible dialogue )

437
00:19:11,397 --> 00:19:13,607
ONE THING
I COULD NEVER FIGURE OUT

438
00:19:13,607 --> 00:19:16,027
WAS WHY HE WANTED
TO STAY WITH ME.

439
00:19:18,237 --> 00:19:19,697
THE OTHER WAS HIM.

440
00:19:20,777 --> 00:19:23,157
ALL THAT TIME TOGETHER...

441
00:19:25,947 --> 00:19:28,037
AND I DIDN’T KNOW HIM AT ALL.

442
00:19:29,457 --> 00:19:32,167
I KNEW AKIHIKO WAS AT HIS CABIN,

443
00:19:32,167 --> 00:19:34,247
BUT I DIDN’T GO THERE
BECAUSE I WANTED TO HELP HIM.

444
00:19:35,877 --> 00:19:38,087
I...

445
00:19:38,087 --> 00:19:40,797
I WENT, BECAUSE I
WANTED TO KILL HIM.

446
00:19:40,797 --> 00:19:42,297
( Asuna gasps )

447
00:19:44,177 --> 00:19:47,727
Rinko: AND THEN,
I DON’T KNOW WHY, BUT I-I...

448
00:19:49,687 --> 00:19:51,187
I COULDN’T DO IT.

449
00:19:52,727 --> 00:19:54,727
HE KNEW WHAT I WAS THINKING

450
00:19:54,727 --> 00:19:56,647
AND THAT I HAD A KNIFE,

451
00:19:56,647 --> 00:19:58,607
BUT HE JUST SMILED AND SAID,

452
00:19:58,607 --> 00:20:02,277
"WHAT AM I GONNA DO WITH YOU?"
LIKE HE ALWAYS DID,

453
00:20:02,277 --> 00:20:04,447
AND THEN HE WENT
BACK TO AINCRAD.

454
00:20:05,617 --> 00:20:07,537
( crying )

455
00:20:09,287 --> 00:20:11,327
OH, GOD. I’M SO SORRY.

456
00:20:11,327 --> 00:20:14,457
( crying )

457
00:20:14,457 --> 00:20:16,877
Asuna: KIRITO AND I
NEVER BLAMED YOU

458
00:20:16,877 --> 00:20:18,917
OR HATED YOU FOR ANYTHING.

459
00:20:18,917 --> 00:20:22,547
TO TELL YOU THE TRUTH,
I CAN’T REALLY SAY

460
00:20:22,547 --> 00:20:24,507
I HATE THE COMMANDER, EITHER.

461
00:20:24,507 --> 00:20:26,767
I-I MEAN AKIHIKO KAYABA.

462
00:20:28,347 --> 00:20:29,767
♪

463
00:20:33,147 --> 00:20:36,397
I’M NOT SAYING HE SHOULD
BE FORGIVEN FOR WHAT HE DID.

464
00:20:36,397 --> 00:20:39,607
HE SHOULDN’T.
A LOT OF LIVES WERE LOST.

465
00:20:39,607 --> 00:20:41,567
BUT STILL--

466
00:20:41,567 --> 00:20:44,067
AND THIS MAY SOUND
A LITTLE SELFISH--

467
00:20:44,067 --> 00:20:45,827
I WOULDN’T TRADE ANYTHING

468
00:20:45,827 --> 00:20:48,407
FOR THE TIME I GOT TO SPEND
LIVING THERE WITH KIRITO.

469
00:20:50,537 --> 00:20:54,497
HONESTLY, TO ME, THOSE WERE
THE BEST DAYS OF MY LIFE.

470
00:20:54,497 --> 00:20:56,457
( Rinko gasps )

471
00:20:56,457 --> 00:20:58,757
Asuna: YES, THE COMMANDER
COMMITTED A CRIME,

472
00:20:58,757 --> 00:21:00,717
AND SO DID KIRITO AND I,

473
00:21:00,717 --> 00:21:02,337
AND YOU DID, TOO.

474
00:21:02,337 --> 00:21:04,007
WE ALL DID SOMETHING WRONG,

475
00:21:04,007 --> 00:21:06,387
AND, IN THE END,
EVEN IF WE’RE PUNISHED,

476
00:21:06,387 --> 00:21:08,927
THERE’S NO WAY TO MAKE IT RIGHT.

477
00:21:08,927 --> 00:21:11,597
I DON’T THINK THE DAY WILL
EVER COME WHEN WE’RE FORGIVEN.

478
00:21:11,597 --> 00:21:14,267
ALL WE CAN DO IS OWN UP TO IT.

479
00:21:14,267 --> 00:21:17,857
THERE’S NO CHOICE BUT
TO FACE OUR SINS AND KEEP GOING.

480
00:21:23,657 --> 00:21:25,567
( footsteps )

481
00:21:28,237 --> 00:21:30,787
Kayaba: COMING ALL
THE WAY OUT HERE?

482
00:21:30,787 --> 00:21:32,707
( scoffs )
WHAT AM I GONNA DO WITH YOU?

483
00:21:33,957 --> 00:21:35,917
( Rinko gasps )

484
00:21:35,917 --> 00:21:38,457
IT’S SO EARLY.

485
00:21:38,457 --> 00:21:40,207
COME BACK TO BED.

486
00:21:41,877 --> 00:21:43,717
( gasps )

487
00:21:46,967 --> 00:21:48,637
( panting )

488
00:21:51,637 --> 00:21:53,347
( sighs )

489
00:21:54,727 --> 00:21:56,937
WAS THAT...

490
00:21:56,937 --> 00:21:58,767
A DREAM?

491
00:22:04,697 --> 00:22:05,947
♪

492
00:22:05,947 --> 00:22:07,617
( singing in Japanese )

493
00:22:42,027 --> 00:22:45,857
♪ THE IRIS TO YOU ♪

